    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d261">

                <pb facs="0509" n="499" xml:id="pg499"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11–1046: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-11-10T07:00:00+08:00">November 10,
                            1946—7 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 9—11:44 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1850. Chinese Government has informed Communist delegation in writing through
                    General Marshall that cease-fire order becomes effective noon November 11 and
                    requests that Committee of Three meet at once.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
